WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.160
The bigger they are, the harder they fall.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.840
Celebrity is a tough business all around,
and the pressures of fame and wealth can be

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.100
too much for some actors to handle.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.410
While these are problems that most people
would envy, these actors might beg to differ.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.080
They came close to derailing their careers,
but we're glad they were able to rebound back

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.340
into the spotlight.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.450
Natalie Portman

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.270
Natalie Portman has never really left the
public eye, but she sees it differently.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:29.380
She told New York Magazine, "I was in the
biggest-grossing movie of the decade, and

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.370
no director wanted to work with me," which
makes it sound like most of Hollywood agreed

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.199
with the hate that hardcore fans had for the
Star Wars prequels.

00:00:36.199 --> 00:00:39.769
"I can't fight a war for you."

00:00:39.769 --> 00:00:41.309
"Jar Jar Binks."

00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:43.350
"Me sir, ya highness?"

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.350
"Yes.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.899
I need your help."

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:50.370
But with the help of some friends in high
places, she bounced back in a series of roles

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.659
in movies like Cold Mountain, Garden State,
Closer, and Black Swan.

00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:58.629
Now, Portman is once again considered one
of Hollywood's top actresses.

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:03.109
She appeared in the first two Thor movies,
and her role in Ex Machina director Alex Garland's

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:07.060
Annihilation suggests she still knows how
to pick a script.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.060
Paul Reubens

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:12.060
You probably know him as Pee-Wee Herman, and
the scandal that derailed his career has been

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.690
a punchline for years.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:19.670
In 1991, Paul Reubens was arrested for "indecent
exposure" inside an "adult theater"...because

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:22.860
apparently, most watch adult films for the
thrilling plots.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.970
In the fallout from the incident, CBS stopped
airing reruns of Pee-wee's Playhouse, and

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.530
Reubens retreated from the public eye for
many years.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.320
After years out of the limelight, Reubens
reclaimed his famous character, donning the

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:38.740
grey suit and red bow-tie once again for the
2016 Netflix film, Pee-Wee's Big Holiday.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.890
Nearly 30 years after the character's last
major film, Big Top Pee-Wee, the new release

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.920
was positively embraced by fans and critics
alike.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.370
Robert Downey, Jr.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:52.200
He had promising beginnings in a number of
critically acclaimed big-budget films, not

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.630
to mention a stint on SNL.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:58.750
But Robert Downey, Jr.'s sudden fame, mixed
with an undiagnosed bipolar disorder, resulted

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:02.350
in a number of drug and alcohol-related arrests
in the late '90s.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:05.950
After cleaning up his act, Downey started
to roll out the hits, appearing in Kiss Kiss

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.550
Bang Bang, Gothika, A Scanner Darkly, and
Tropic Thunder.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:13.510
He's most known for his ongoing lead roles
in Guy Ritchie's Sherlock Holmes series and

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:17.770
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe as Tony Stark,
also known as Iron Man.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:21.609
Nothing like starring in a multi-billion dollar
franchise to pull you out of a little personal

00:02:21.609 --> 00:02:22.609
slump, huh?

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:23.609
Mike Tyson

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:28.299
The terrifying Tyson didn't start his career
as an actor, but found a renaissance as one.

00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:32.940
Known best as a boxing champion, Tyson's controversial
life has included multiple accusations of

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.299
violence against women, longtime drug and
alcohol abuse...

00:02:36.299 --> 00:02:38.739
"But I knew when I was in that court, and
when I was gonna get that verdict, I knew

00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:40.380
the verdict was gonna be guilty."

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:45.519
...and biting off a chunk of Evander Holyfield's
ear in their 1997 rematch.

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:49.280
After retreating from the public eye in shame,
Tyson found a new life by appearing in The

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.389
Hangover from 2009.

00:02:51.389 --> 00:02:55.540
Since then, he got his own cartoon series,
Mike Tyson Mysteries.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.560
Holyfield and Tyson appeared together in a
post-credits scene during the 2013 boxing

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.730
movie, Grudge Match.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:05.329
You can also catch Tyson taking on martial
arts and action star Donnie Yen in Ip Man

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:06.519
3.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.870
Drew Barrymore

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.469
Child actress Drew Barrymore's career was
almost over before it began.

00:03:11.469 --> 00:03:13.330
After starring in the 1982 hit E.T.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:18.290
at age seven, Barrymore became notorious for
abusing alcohol, marijuana and cocaine—by

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:21.200
her own admission, starting at the age of
eight.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.980
Fortunately, thanks to rehab, and the unlikely
help of a family friend...

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.610
"I had to live with David Crosby for two months."

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.480
"Which is crazy because David had his own
problems."

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.650
"I know he's, he was an interesting character
in itself."

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:36.909
...Barrymore found sobriety and started her
wildly successful second act, starring in

00:03:36.909 --> 00:03:40.349
movies like Scream, The Wedding Singer, and
Never Been Kissed.

00:03:40.349 --> 00:03:43.930
Barrymore also focuses on her family and charity
work while appearing in ads as one of the

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.260
faces of CoverGirl.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.480
But that doesn't mean she's slowing down in
terms of acting, despite the fact that she

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.860
only took four roles from 2009 to 2016.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.260
Because if she could come back from being
a teenage addict and the trainwreck that was

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:59.239
Charlie's Angels: Full Throttle, she can come
back from anything.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.239
Fred Willard

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:04.950
Comedian and actor Fred Willard's career was
marked by nothing but funny movies...until

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.640
his 2012 arrest for a "lewd act" in an adult
theater.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.879
The arrest cost him his job hosting Market
Warriors, but Willard was quick to recover

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:17.209
after an honest interview on Late Night with
Jimmy Fallon in which he showcased his legendary

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:18.209
sense of humor:

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:19.209
"Jimmy!

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:20.209
What do you wanna talk about first?"

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:27.000
"Ya know, let me say this, it's the last time
I'm gonna listen to my wife when she says

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.129
why don't you go out and see a movie."

00:04:29.129 --> 00:04:34.720
Since then, he's appeared in Anchorman 2:
The Legend Continues, Fifty Shades of Black,

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:39.139
and a handful of television roles, and most
likely discovered the joys of "private browsing

00:04:39.139 --> 00:04:40.139
mode."

00:04:40.139 --> 00:04:41.139
Mickey Rourke

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:46.010
Former boxer and semi-reluctant actor Mickey
Rourke enjoyed a successful career...until

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:51.260
he was arrested for spousal abuse in 1994
after assaulting his then-wife Carré Otis.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:55.910
Oh yeah, and he was responsible for her getting
accidentally shot in the chest once, too.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:59.580
Just a guess, but he probably didn't get the
World's Best Husband mug that Christmas.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:05.110
As a result, Rourke almost gave up the spotlight
completely, returning to boxing, then to acting,

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.440
then to boxing again—Wait, is he boxing
in a kilt?

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:13.810
Anyway, he bounced back to acting for good
with a lead role in 2005's Sin City:

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.180
"Let's go."

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:19.960
This major return, which he attributes to
his manager and his dogs, led to Rourke appearing

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.740
in The Wrestler, Iron Man 2, and The Expendables.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:24.979
Rob Lowe

00:05:24.979 --> 00:05:29.240
In the age of Kardashians, it's hard to remember
that a sex tape could once ruin someone's

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.889
career...and Rob Lowe had one of the first.

00:05:31.889 --> 00:05:35.960
Only a few years into his career, Lowe was
filmed with at least three different women,

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:40.569
one of whom was barely above legal age, sparking
a wave of media controversy when the tape

00:05:40.569 --> 00:05:43.000
was made available for sale against his will.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.800
Lowe quickly recovered, thanks to the apparent
indifference of Hollywood, and a willingness

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.710
to own up to the situation.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:52.889
During the years since he rebounded from his
scandal, Lowe has appeared in dozens of movies,

00:05:52.889 --> 00:05:56.720
including the Cameron Diaz and Jason Segel
movie, Sex Tape, which was a nice meta joke

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.140
in the form of stunt casting.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:02.990
Even more impressive, his television resume
spans hundreds of episodes across dozens of

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:08.300
noteworthy shows, including the likes of The
West Wing, Parks and Recreation, Californication,

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.539
Moonbeam City, and The Grinder.

00:06:10.539 --> 00:06:11.600
Thanks for watching!

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.250
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:18.550
And leave us a comment to let us know which
actors you think we should've added to the

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:19.050
list...

